STEPS IN SUMMARY:
        - Run the a perl production script, with the GRID option: $ perl submit_feldman_cousins_fitting_job_numu_grid
		This creates a few files:
			a lot of .sh files that setup the enviroment and run the script (these are like .pbs files)
			a lot of .jdl files that send the files to the grid 	
			a single .sh file that sets up your proxy, creates the tar ball, and submits all the jobs
        - Run the .sh single script: $ ./fc.sh
        - Insert GRID password
		All jobs have now been sent (eventually...)
        - glite-wms-job-status -i $tag.jid -o stats
		To see the status of the jobs (press "a" to get the status of all)
	- $T2KOSCANA/production/grid/check_status.py
		To see the status of the jobs summarised
        - glite-wms-job-output --dir ./outputs/ -i $tag.jid 
		To get the outputs (if you sent 1000s, better to wait for all of them to finish and retrieve all of them at once)




# view proxy info
myproxy-info -d
voms-proxy-info



A template on how to add GRID options to production scripts is in: submit_toyexpt_fitting_job_xml
Important things to note are:

 - the ouput sandbox needs to be specified exactly. Unfortunately wildcards don't work (e.g. *.root), so you need to be careful to get back all you need

 - the only macros copied are fit/toymc/* and fit/stat/* - if you need any from anywhere else, remember to copy them

The template isn't quite ready for full production - there is a problem with proxy delegation not always working. I'm chasing this up (and specifying ROOT version on worker nodes) today, hope to be able to start grid production this evening


UPDATES APRIL 2013

In order to be able to retrieve the job output (*.root) after the proxy has expired, i.e. after 24 hours, the job is copying the .root file at the end of the execution in my directory at the grid, /grid/t2k.org/contrib/lorena/outputs/ (please create your own folder there), via lcg-cr commands. It is not necessary then to check status and retrieve output files individually. Instead one just need to run the script retrieve_GRID_outputs.sh. This script just list the files in the outputs directory (please edit it to list the jobs in your own folder), copy all files and delete them from the grid. Important: you need a "production" role to be able to write in the grid.

TIER2

Some changes are necessary for working in the Tier2 CE, concerning essentially environmental variables and software. It is actually much easier indeed, as the code can be read and used from /opt/..., so we don't need to send anymore the tar ball with the code, compile, delete, etc. But since it is so much different from the way we have to work on the rest of CE, I keep a sample submission script in both ways. These examples scripts, with latest updates, are:

production/grid/submit_sensitivity_study_joint_grid_1D -> working for IC farm
production/grid/submit_sensitivity_study_joint_grid_1D_Tier2 -> working for RAL PP Tier2 farm

PROXY DELEGATION

The following should work to delegate proxy and get it renewed every 12 hours (for next four months) so that jobs can keep running after the usual 24 hours.

First do:
myproxy-init -n -d -c 672 -s lcgrbp01.gridpp.rl.ac.uk
you have to do this once every 4 weeks, it should delegate to proxy to myproxyserver at RAL (gridpp)
Then, changes added in autowms.conf to use the same myproxyserver and wms gridpp so that they trust each other. 
When submitting jobs the voms-proxy-init command line to be used is the same.
This should work now to be able to run jobs for > 24 hours - testing it.



#CREATE DIRECTORY
lfc-mkdir /grid/t2k.org/nd280/contrib/dealtry/DIR

#DELETE DIRECTORY
#first need to delete all files
lcg-del  -v --vo t2k.org -a lfn:/grid/t2k.org/nd280/contrib/dealtry/DIR/FILENAME
#then delete the directory
lfc-rm -r /grid/t2k.org/nd280/contrib/dealtry/DIR
